  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The stripes are worked by switching yarn colours every 2 rounds. Use a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "colour-change-ze"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "colour change"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " at the start of each stripe round. Carry the unused colour loosely inside rather than cutting each time to save ends. All pieces start with a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring-ze"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Yarn and yarn amounts"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "You need approx. 34 g total: roughly half white and half black DK."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Head"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work a 6 cm by 8 cm oval head in alternating 2-round stripes (18 rounds). Fit "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "safety-eyes-ze"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "safety eyes"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " at round 8."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Body"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work a 8 cm diameter by 10 cm cylinder in 2-round stripes (28 rounds). Stuff firmly so the body is rigid enough for the legs to support it."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Legs (make 4)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work a 2.5 cm diameter by 7 cm capsule per leg in 2-round stripes. Use "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "dc2tog-ze"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "dc2tog"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " for the decrease rounds (18 rounds)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ears (make 2)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work a 2 cm by 3 cm oval flat in white with a black inner oval sewn on."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Mane"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cut 4 cm lengths of black yarn. Fold each in half and loop through rounds along the top of the head and neck using a crochet hook."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Assembly"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pin all four legs to the body base before sewing to confirm the zebra stands flat. Use "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "ladder-stitch-ze"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "ladder stitch"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " to attach legs. Sew head to the body front."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The amigurumi giraffe uses the same cylinder body with a long neck piece added."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}